# Tailwind-First Styling — Mandatory

Style UI with **Tailwind utility classes** first. Custom CSS in `globals.css` or standalone stylesheets is **not allowed** for component-level layout, spacing, color, typography, or shadows unless an exception below applies.

## Default approach

1. **Component markup** — `className={cn("...", className)}` with Tailwind + project tokens (`mainColor`, `thirdColor`, `darkColor`, `lightColor`, `rounded-main`, `rounded-secondary`, …).
2. **Layout helpers** — reuse `@utility` classes from `globals.css`: `margin`, `spacing`, `left-padding`, `right-padding`, `bg-root`.
3. **shadcn/ui** — override via `className` / `classNames`, **not** `unstyled: true` + bespoke CSS blocks.
4. **`cn()`** — merge conditional classes; extract repeated strings to `const` in the same file when reused.

## Allowed custom CSS (exceptions only)

- **Global design tokens** — `@theme` / `@theme inline` in `globals.css`
- **Cross-cutting utilities** already defined (`margin`, `spacing`, rounded-out helpers) when Tailwind alone is awkward
- **`@keyframes`** only when no Tailwind / `tw-animate` equivalent exists

## Do not

- Add new `.feature-name { … }` blocks in `globals.css` for a single component
- Inline `<style>` tags or CSS modules for page UI unless explicitly requested
- Invent a parallel token system — extend existing `@theme` colors/radii if needed

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — one-off globals.css class for a section
// .home-cta { padding: 4rem; background: #6b5ab1; }

// ✅ GOOD
<section className="spacing margin rounded-main bg-mainColor text-white">…</section>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hardcode hex that already exists as a token
<div className="bg-[#6b5ab1]" />

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="bg-mainColor" />
```
